# Environment Variables

## Required for Production

### Form Submission API
```
VITE_FORM_API_URL=https://your-backend-api.com/api/signup
```
Set this to your backend API endpoint that will handle form submissions.

**Recommended services:**
- Formspree: https://formspree.io (easiest setup)
- EmailJS: https://www.emailjs.com
- Mailchimp API: for email list management
- SendGrid API: for email notifications
- Custom backend: Node.js/Express, Python/Flask, etc.

**Example Formspree setup:**
```
VITE_FORM_API_URL=https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_FORM_ID
```

### Instagram Feed (Optional)
```
INSTAGRAM_APP_ID=your_instagram_app_id
INSTAGRAM_APP_SECRET=your_instagram_app_secret
INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_long_lived_access_token
CRON_SECRET=random_secret_for_manual_refresh_endpoint
```
Get app credentials from the Meta Developer Console after setting up the Instagram API with Instagram Login.
Tutorial: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/instagram-platform/instagram-api-with-instagram-login/business-login/

For automatic token refresh on Render, also set:
```
RENDER_API_KEY=your_render_api_key
RENDER_SERVICE_ID=srv_your_web_service_id
RENDER_CRON_SERVICE_ID=srv_your_cron_service_id
```

**Important:** Keep these server-side only (no `VITE_` prefix). The access token is used by `/api/instagram` and is never exposed to the browser.

## Development

Copy this file to `.env` and add your values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

## Production Deployment

Set these environment variables in your hosting platform:
- Render: Dashboard > Environment > Environment Variables
- Vercel / Netlify: only needed if you deploy the Node server that serves `/api/instagram`

## Notes

- `VITE_` variables are embedded in the client bundle — never use that prefix for secrets
- Never commit `.env` or any file containing actual secrets
- Instagram long-lived tokens expire after ~60 days; refresh them before expiry
